      "writtenOn": "2024-07-23T23:50:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can we make most of these configs common among all the mtlrvp tests?\n\nfor example, does `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_HOOKS\u003dn` need to be\nspecific to some tests? wouldn\u0027t it be better if all tests for\na particular board run against a substantially similar config\nthat is representative of the real board?",
      "parentUuid": "ef6f21f7_ab48b165",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "82eb34284002daee8ae68fb5bba840fd3a7ece79",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c4b585b_48e6db0a",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/intelrvp/testcase.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1570962
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-25T00:04:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With that approach we will have to include all the dtsi files in all the tests and rather than it testing a particular module, it would become a test for big blob. Making change to one test configs might fail all other tests too. They wont remain isolated. Does it make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "337c7f84_a3feca57",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "82eb34284002daee8ae68fb5bba840fd3a7ece79",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86e62abf_27b413b3",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/intelrvp/testcase.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-25T02:54:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "by enabling common configs and including the relevant dts*,\nyou have a representative RVP EC image running in the emulator.\nthat should provide a more predictable environment for running\nspecific unit tests.\n\nif you look at `.../handler.log` files for various tests,\nyou\u0027ll see the EC booting up and running some unrealistic\ninit code that probably doesn\u0027t make sense. the unit\ntest will run before or after this code depending on how\nthe test is set up.... my concern with this is that the test\ninevitably doesn\u0027t actually run in isolation as a unit test - it\nstill runs in a \"booted\" EC image in the emulator.",
      "parentUuid": "9c4b585b_48e6db0a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 33
      },
